 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One unit of about 170 s: the reciter joins every verse from 102 to 108. A seal for holding fast together (no rope drawn), a house for brotherhood, two_paths for right and wrong, wind for the scattering of those who split. The Day (106-107): no faces drawn, nothing literal; only light on «رحمة» (mercy). Nothing for the Fire (103:22-25). 103: short-word flag at 17 (listen). STAGING v4: 102: believers bow on «اتقوا» and pray at dawn (prostration on «مسلمون»). 103: two groups who were enemies (Al-Muyassar: before Islam) turn their backs on each other on 103:12-13, turn back on «فألف», one walks over to the other on «فأصبحتم» (house plate) and both raise their hands on «إخوانا»; nothing drawn for the pit of the Fire, a soft light on «فأنقذكم» (Al-Muyassar: He guided you by Islam). 104: «منكم أمة» = part of the believers (b) call to good (speak), enjoin (point) and forbid (shake_head) before people (p). 105: the earlier communities who split (Al-Muyassar: the People of the Book): a group enters, walks apart (105:4-5) and argues (speak / shake_head); they stay on stage, nothing drawn for the punishment. 106-107 (the Day) stay ambient. 108: believers read the Quran in a prayer hall (the Prophet, addressed by «عليك», is never shown); geometric only on the Name."
 },
